export const pkUnit02CommonInfoMarkdown: LocalizedText = {
  "en": "# PK Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home — Common Info\n\n## 1. Unit Theme Overview\n\nPK Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home helps children connect familiar people, home routines, classroom friendship, and early social role play. Compared with PG, PK children can participate in more intentional pretend play, simple choice responses, short phrase imitation, and more stable turn-taking. The unit still remains non-language developmental work, not a formal speaking unit.\n\nChildren revisit family members, friends, teacher, home, room, bed, and familiar objects such as toy, book, bag, blanket, and photo. They use these words through photos, dolls, puppets, home-corner play, construction, care routines, creative expression, music, and PSED routines.\n\nThe unit should protect emotional safety. Children may use their own family photos where appropriate, but they should not be required to explain their family, compare family structures, or produce personal family sentences. Generic dolls, puppets, picture cards, and home-corner props are sufficient.\n\n## 2. Unit Language\n\n### PK Core Vocabulary\n\n```text\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ family ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ home ｜ house ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ blanket ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ photo ｜ door ｜ chair ｜ table\n```\n\n### Functional Teacher Chunks\n\n```text\nThis is Mum. ｜ This is Dad. ｜ This is Baby. ｜ Show me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Baby. ｜ Who is this? ｜ Mum or Dad? ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Go home. ｜ Come in. ｜ Knock, knock. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad. ｜ My friend. ｜ Sit with your friend. ｜ Your turn. ｜ Thank you.\n```\n\n## 3. Weekly Subthemes\n\n### Week 1: My Family People\n\nChildren revisit Mum, Dad, Baby, family, and photo through cards, puppets, dolls, songs, and picture routines. The focus is recognition, matching, showing, pointing, choosing, and optional short naming.\n\n### Week 2: My Home and My Room\n\nChildren explore home, house, room, bed, blanket, chair, table, and door through home-corner play, block homes, doll beds, and care routines.\n\n### Week 3: My Friend Visits\n\nChildren connect home language with friendship routines: friend comes in, friend sits, friend shares a toy, friend waits, and friend says bye-bye.\n\n### Week 4: Family, Friend and Home Routines\n\nChildren integrate family, friend, home, bed, photo, toy, book, and goodbye routines through longer but still simple sequences: family comes home, Baby sleeps, friend visits, toys go home, and everyone says bye-bye.\n\n## 4. Teacher Input Pool\n\n### Family and Relationship Input\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ family ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ photo ｜ this is Mum ｜ this is Dad ｜ this is Baby ｜ my friend ｜ family photo\n\n### Home and Object Input\n\nhome ｜ house ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ blanket ｜ chair ｜ table ｜ door ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ toy ｜ go home ｜ come in ｜ in bed ｜ on the bed\n\n### Social and Routine Input\n\nshow ｜ point ｜ choose ｜ give ｜ take ｜ put ｜ sit ｜ wait ｜ your turn ｜ thank you ｜ knock knock ｜ bye-bye ｜ all done ｜ clean up\n\n### Teacher Routine Language\n\nLook at the photo. ｜ Show me Mum. ｜ Point to Baby. ｜ Mum or Dad? ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Knock, knock. ｜ Come in. ｜ Sit with your friend. ｜ Wait. ｜ Your turn. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bye-bye. ｜ Thank you. ｜ Good job.\n\n## 5. Expected PK Response Modes\n\nChildren may respond by looking, pointing, touching, choosing between two family cards, matching a photo or picture to a puppet, saying or attempting `Mum`, `Dad`, `Baby`, or `friend`, giving an object to a puppet, putting Baby in bed, covering Baby with a blanket, moving a family figure into a home, knocking on a home door, saying or gesturing bye-bye, waiting briefly, sharing a toy with a friend, or using short fixed chunks such as `My friend`, `Come in`, `Thank you`, or `Bye-bye` when ready.\n\nChildren are not expected to explain family relationships, describe their own family, answer full personal questions, produce full sentences such as `This is my mother`, identify extended family members, or describe rooms and homes in detail.\n\n## 6. Theme Songs / Chants\n\n### Core Songs\n\nMy Teddy Bear  \nPeekaboo  \nPeekaboo Playground  \nHide And Seek  \nPeekaboo, I Love You  \nBaby Shark  \nThe More We Get Together  \nI Like You  \nSkidamarink  \nSay Cheese!  \nWhere Is Baby  \nFinger Family\n\n### Use of Songs\n\nSongs should support family recognition, peekaboo, baby-care routines, friendship, photo play, home routines, and goodbye transitions. Children may sing familiar repeated words when ready, but gesture, movement, hiding/revealing, rocking Baby, passing Teddy, and waving remain acceptable participation.\n\n## 7. Resource Opportunities\n\n### Useful EASTIE Spaces\n\nClassroom  \nHome corner / pretend-play area  \nBook corner  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PK classroom  \nTheatre / dramatic play space  \nArt classroom  \nConstruction / block room  \nMusic classroom  \nCircle-time area / mat area  \nTable activity area\n\n### Useful Materials\n\nFamily photo cards  \nGeneric family picture cards  \nChild photos where appropriate  \nDolls / baby dolls  \nDoll beds  \nBlankets  \nDoll strollers  \nToy kitchen  \nToy food  \nToy phone  \nToy house  \nDollhouse furniture  \nPuppets  \nFinger puppets  \nTeddy bears  \nBags  \nBooks  \nBaskets  \nBlocks  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nLego / Duplo bricks  \nScarves / cloths  \nVisual routine cards  \nFriend cards  \nTurn-taking objects\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities\n\nHome-corner play can support longer pretend sequences than PG. Construction materials can support building home, room, door, and bed spaces. Art can support family photo frames, home collages, and friend displays. Music and theatre spaces can support friend visits, family songs, and simple dramatic routines.\n\n## 8. Boundary Notes\n\nThis unit should not become a family-tree lesson. Extended family vocabulary is not a PK baseline requirement.\n\nThis unit should not require children to disclose or compare their own family. Use generic family materials when needed.\n\nThis unit should not require full sentence output. `This is Mum`, `My friend`, `Come in`, or `Bye-bye` may be supported as short chunks, but action response remains valid.\n\nThis unit should not turn home vocabulary into room-description tasks. Home and room are experienced through props, movement, construction, and pretend care.\n\n## 9. Unit-Level Observation Focus\n\nTeachers observe whether children recognise and respond to family and friend words, participate in home and baby-care routines, use or attempt short chunks when ready, engage in simple home-corner pretend play, wait and take turns with friends, connect objects with people and places, and show emotional security when home/family themes are introduced.\n\nObservation should focus on relational awareness, symbolic play, social participation, routine response, emotional safety, and readiness-based language attempts rather than full verbal description.\n",
  "zh": "# PK Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home — Common Info｜PK 单元 2：我的家人、朋友与家 — 通用信息\n\n## 1. Unit Theme Overview｜单元主题概览\n\nPK 单元 2：我的家人、朋友与家帮助儿童把熟悉的人、家庭常规、课堂友谊和早期社交角色游戏连接起来。和 PG 相比，PK 儿童可以参与更有意识的假装游戏、简单的选择回应、简短的短语模仿，以及更稳定的轮流。本单元仍然是非语言发展工作，不是正式的口语课。\n\n儿童重新接触家庭成员、朋友、教师、家、房间、床，以及熟悉的物品，例如玩具、书、包、毛毯和照片。他们通过照片、娃娃、木偶、家庭角游戏、建构、照护常规、创意表达、音乐和 PSED 常规来使用这些词。\n\n本单元应保护情感安全。儿童在合适的时候可以使用自己的家庭照片，但不应被要求解释自己的家庭、比较家庭结构或产出个人家庭句。通用娃娃、木偶、图片卡和家庭角道具已足够。\n\n## 2. Unit Language｜单元语言\n\n### PK Core Vocabulary｜PK 核心词汇\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ family ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ home ｜ house ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ blanket ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ photo ｜ door ｜ chair ｜ table\n\n### Functional Teacher Chunks｜实用教师句块\n\nThis is Mum. ｜ This is Dad. ｜ This is Baby. ｜ Show me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Baby. ｜ Who is this? ｜ Mum or Dad? ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Go home. ｜ Come in. ｜ Knock, knock. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad. ｜ My friend. ｜ Sit with your friend. ｜ Your turn. ｜ Thank you.\n\n## 3. Weekly Subthemes｜周次子主题\n\n### Week 1: My Family People｜第一周：我的家人\n\n儿童通过卡片、木偶、娃娃、歌曲和图片常规重新接触妈妈、爸爸、宝宝、家庭和照片。重点是识别、匹配、展示、指、选择和可选的简短命名。\n\n### Week 2: My Home and My Room｜第二周：我的家与我的房间\n\n儿童通过家庭角游戏、积木家、娃娃床和照护常规来探索家、房子、房间、床、毛毯、椅子、桌子和门。\n\n### Week 3: My Friend Visits｜第三周：朋友来访\n\n儿童把家的语言和友谊常规连接起来：朋友进来、朋友坐下、朋友分享一个玩具、朋友等待、朋友说再见。\n\n### Week 4: Family, Friend and Home Routines｜第四周：家庭、朋友与家常规\n\n儿童通过更长但仍然简单的序列把家庭、朋友、家、床、照片、玩具、书和再见常规整合起来：家人回家、宝宝睡觉、朋友来访、玩具回家、大家说再见。\n\n## 4. Teacher Input Pool｜教师输入库\n\n### Family and Relationship Input｜家庭与关系输入\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ family ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ photo ｜ this is Mum ｜ this is Dad ｜ this is Baby ｜ my friend ｜ family photo\n\n### Home and Object Input｜家与物品输入\n\nhome ｜ house ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ blanket ｜ chair ｜ table ｜ door ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ toy ｜ go home ｜ come in ｜ in bed ｜ on the bed\n\n### Social and Routine Input｜社交与常规输入\n\nshow ｜ point ｜ choose ｜ give ｜ take ｜ put ｜ sit ｜ wait ｜ your turn ｜ thank you ｜ knock knock ｜ bye-bye ｜ all done ｜ clean up\n\n### Teacher Routine Language｜教师常规语言\n\nLook at the photo. ｜ Show me Mum. ｜ Point to Baby. ｜ Mum or Dad? ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Knock, knock. ｜ Come in. ｜ Sit with your friend. ｜ Wait. ｜ Your turn. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bye-bye. ｜ Thank you. ｜ Good job.\n\n## 5. Expected PK Response Modes｜预期 PK 反应方式\n\n儿童可能通过以下方式反应：看、指、触摸、在两张家庭卡之间选择、把照片或图片和木偶匹配、在准备好时说或尝试 `Mum`、`Dad`、`Baby` 或 `friend`、把物品给木偶、把宝宝放进床里、用毛毯盖住宝宝、把一个家庭小人偶移入一个家、敲一扇家的门、说或用动作示意再见、短暂等待、和朋友分享一个玩具，或在准备好时使用简短固定句块，例如 `My friend`、`Come in`、`Thank you`、`Bye-bye`。\n\n不要求儿童解释家庭关系、描述自己的家庭、回答完整的个人问题、产出完整句子例如 `This is my mother`、识别大家庭成员，或详细描述房间和家。\n\n## 6. Core Unit Songs｜单元核心歌曲\n\n### Core Songs｜核心歌曲\n\nMy Teddy Bear  \nPeekaboo  \nPeekaboo Playground  \nHide And Seek  \nPeekaboo, I Love You  \nBaby Shark  \nThe More We Get Together  \nI Like You  \nSkidamarink  \nSay Cheese!  \nWhere Is Baby  \nFinger Family\n\n### Use of Songs｜歌曲的使用\n\n歌曲应当支持家庭识别、躲猫猫、宝宝照护常规、友谊、照片游戏、家庭常规和再见过渡。儿童在准备好时可以唱熟悉的重复词，但手势、动作、躲藏／揭示、摇宝宝、传递泰迪、挥手仍是可接受的参与。\n\n## 7. Resource Opportunities｜资源机会\n\n### Useful EASTIE Spaces｜可用 EASTIE 空间\n\nClassroom  \nHome corner / pretend-play area  \nBook corner  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PK classroom  \nTheatre / dramatic play space  \nArt classroom  \nConstruction / block room  \nMusic classroom  \nCircle-time area / mat area  \nTable activity area\n\n### Useful Materials｜可用材料\n\nFamily photo cards  \nGeneric family picture cards  \nChild photos where appropriate  \nDolls / baby dolls  \nDoll beds  \nBlankets  \nDoll strollers  \nToy kitchen  \nToy food  \nToy phone  \nToy house  \nDollhouse furniture  \nPuppets  \nFinger puppets  \nTeddy bears  \nBags  \nBooks  \nBaskets  \nBlocks  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nLego / Duplo bricks  \nScarves / cloths  \nVisual routine cards  \nFriend cards  \nTurn-taking objects\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities｜拓展资源机会\n\n家庭角游戏可以支持比 PG 更长的假装序列。建构材料可以支持搭建家、房间、门和床的空间。艺术可以支持家庭相框、家庭拼贴和朋友展示。音乐和剧场空间可以支持朋友来访、家庭歌曲和简单的戏剧常规。\n\n## 8. Boundary Notes｜边界说明\n\n本单元不应变成家谱课。大家庭词汇不是 PK 基线要求。\n\n本单元不应要求儿童披露或比较自己的家庭。需要时使用通用家庭材料。\n\n本单元不应要求完整句子输出。\"This is Mum\"、\"My friend\"、\"Come in\" 或 \"Bye-bye\" 可以作为简短句块支持，但动作反应仍有效。\n\n本单元不应把家词汇变成房间描述任务。家和房间通过道具、动作、建构和假装照护来体验。\n\n## 9. Unit-Level Observation Focus｜单元观察重点\n\n教师观察儿童是否识别并回应家庭和朋友词、参与家和宝宝照护常规、在准备好时使用或尝试简短句块、参与简单的家庭角假装游戏、和朋友等待与轮流、把物品和人以及地方连接、以及在家／家庭主题引入时显示出情感安全感。\n\n观察应聚焦于关系意识、象征性游戏、社交参与、常规反应、情感安全和准备度导向的语言尝试，而非完整口头描述。"
};

